# F1 2026 Season Archive

A dedicated workspace for analysing the 2026 Formula 1 season: the first year of the new technical regulations. This README is the season's "source of truth": context, rules, teams, how the data is organised, and a running log of insights so the work is still understandable years from now.

> **Snapshot date:** 12 October 2026 (after the Singapore GP weekend, 6 races to go).
> Items marked **(verify)** come from memory or secondary sources. Check them against the FIA regulations or official F1 data before relying on them in analysis.

---

## 1. Why 2026 matters

2026 is a reset season. Almost everything that shaped 2022-2025 changed at once:

- New power unit rules (electrical power roughly equal to combustion power)
- Active aerodynamics instead of DRS
- Smaller, lighter cars
- Fully sustainable fuel
- Two new manufacturers entering or returning: Audi (taking over Sauber) and Cadillac (new 11th team)
- Honda returning as works supplier to Aston Martin, Red Bull building its own PU with Ford, Alpine switching to Mercedes customer engines

The pecking order was shuffled. Mercedes has dominated, a 19-year-old (Kimi Antonelli) leads the championship, and Ferrari has been the main challenger. This is the dataset to study "how a rules reset changes a sport".

