## 5. Repository layout

Suggested structure for the `2026/` folder inside the telemetry repo:

```
2026/
├── README.md                  <- this file
├── docs/
│   ├── regulations.md         <- deeper notes on technical/sporting rules
│   ├── season_log.md          <- race-by-race notes (see section 7)
│   ├── insights.md            <- findings log (see section 8)
│   └── glossary.md            <- terms (clipping, X-mode, etc.)
├── data/
│   ├── raw/                   <- untouched downloads (never edit)
│   ├── interim/               <- cleaned/aligned data
│   ├── processed/             <- analysis-ready tables (parquet/csv)
│   └── external/              <- standings, calendar, regs PDFs
├── notebooks/
│   ├── 00_data_check.ipynb
│   ├── 01_energy_deployment.ipynb
│   ├── 02_active_aero_modes.ipynb
│   └── ...
├── src/
│   ├── loaders.py             <- session loading and caching
│   ├── features.py            <- lap/corner/straight feature extraction
│   ├── plots.py               <- shared plot style
│   └── utils.py
├── projects/
│   ├── energy_management/
│   ├── overtake_mode/
│   └── teammate_battles/
├── reports/
│   └── figures/
└── environment.yml (or requirements.txt)
```

Conventions:
- **Raw data is immutable.** Everything downstream must be reproducible from `raw/`.
- Name notebooks with a numeric prefix and keep one question per notebook.
- Save figures with the session key in the filename, e.g. `2026_R17_SIN_Q_ANT_vs_RUS.png`.
- Record library versions (see section 9) because APIs and channel names change.

